    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "By default, "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " implementations eagerly create and configure all "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "singleton"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "core/beans/factory-scopes.html#beans-factory-scopes-singleton"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " beans as part of the initialization process. Generally, this pre-instantiation is desirable, because errors in the configuration or surrounding environment are discovered immediately, as opposed to hours or even days later. When this behavior is not desirable, you can prevent pre-instantiation of a singleton bean by marking the bean definition as being lazy-initialized. A lazy-initialized bean tells the IoC container to create a bean instance when it is first requested, rather than at startup."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "This behavior is controlled by the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Lazy"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " annotation or in XML the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "lazy-init"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " attribute on the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<bean/>"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " element, as the following example shows:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "include-code::./ApplicationConfiguration[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "When the preceding configuration is consumed by an "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "lazy"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " bean is not eagerly pre-instantiated when the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " starts, whereas the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "notLazy"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " one is eagerly pre-instantiated."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "However, when a lazy-initialized bean is a dependency of a singleton bean that is not lazy-initialized, the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " creates the lazy-initialized bean at startup, because it must satisfy the singleton’s dependencies. The lazy-initialized bean is injected into a singleton bean elsewhere that is not lazy-initialized."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "You can also control lazy-initialization for a set of beans by using the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Lazy"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " annotation on your "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Configuration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " annotated class or in XML using the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
